## The drivers

A scenario in WaterPath is defined by changing one or more *drivers of contamination*: the model inputs that determine how many pathogens are produced, how many of them reach surface water, and how many people are exposed to them. The drivers below are the ones that were parametrized in the context of this case study.

{% for note in driver_notes %}
- **{{ note.name }}.** {{ note.description }}
{% endfor %}

Each scenario chapter walks through these drivers in turn, reports how the scenario differs from the baseline, and then shows the resulting emissions, river concentrations and health risk.
